a sentencing hearing begins this morning  for a former police officer convicted of  manslaughter after shooting a black  woman in her home Aaron Dean faces up to  20 years in prison for the killing  recorded on police body cam video Dean  was charged with murder for shooting at  Tiana Jefferson through a window while  investigating a call from a concerned  neighbor Omar via Franca first covered  this story in 2019 and has our report on  yesterday's verdict  wait for Omar's package there this is  the jury find the defendant Aaron York  Dean guilty of the offensive  manslaughter former Fort Worth police  officer Aaron Dean showed no emotion as  the verdict was read it comes more than  three years after Dean shot 28 year old  to Tatiana Jefferson inside her home  officers came to her home after a  neighbor reported Jefferson's door was  open body cam video showed officers  responding but never identifying  themselves  seconds after Dean spots Jefferson  through her window put your hands up  show me your answer  she was shot as her then eight-year-old  nephew stood watching Dean later  resigned and on the stand argued he was  acting in self-defense I just saw the  silhouette of the person and the gun I  don't recall seeing hands but I did see  that weapon pointed at me but  Jefferson's nephew now 11 years old told  a different story I was thinking is it a  dream she was crying just shaking he  testified his aunt went to the window  after hearing a noise outside and said  she did not Point her gun before she was  shot and fell to the ground if you  remember if she had the gun up or down  down  down are you sure she didn't have it up  at all  he testified the door was only open  because they burned hamburgers and  wanted to air out the house manslaughter  is without the intent to kill he  intended to kill her family and friends  say the manslaughter conviction is not  enough totally disappointed because  Justice have not been served for CBS  mornings I'm Omar villafranca 